Hi everyone,

I've currently got an output from NetLogo in a CSV file, but the formatting of the data is a bit strange. I need some help getting it into a usable format in R, but I can't quite figure out how to get it there. I've gotten partway using tidyr::gather, but I need a bit more help.

Here's the output I get:

Run 1 1 2 2 3 3 4
MovementOdds 20 20 20 20 20 20 20
Infection Status uninfecteds infecteds uninfecteds infecteds uninfecteds infecteds uninfecteds
70 0 70 0 70 0 70
70 0 69 0 69 0 70
70 0 67 0 67 0 69
69 0 66 0 66 0 69
69 0 65 0 66 0 66
68 0 63 0 65 0 65
68 0 63 0 65 0 64
68 0 63 0 65 0 64

Each of the numerical values below represent a count of individuals, and each step down a column represents a time step.

I would like to have the data formatted like this, in the end:

Time Run MovementOdds Infection Count
1 1 20  uninfecteds 70
2 1 20  uninfecteds 70
3 1 20  uninfecteds 70
4 1 20  uninfecteds 69
5 1 20  uninfecteds 69
6 1 20  uninfecteds 68
7 1 20  uninfecteds 68
8 1 20  uninfecteds 68
9 1 20  uninfecteds 68
10 1 20  uninfecteds 67

Where Run is used to organize the data.

I can get the data tidy based on Run if I don't include infection status or movement odds, but I just can't figure out how to get it to work when those two variables are included as rows. I'm not sure if this will involve pure R trickery or if some of the reshaping should be done in Excel prior to reading it to R.

Any help would be appreciated- if someone needs an actual Excel file to goof around with rather than the abbreviated table I provided, just let me know.

Many thanks,

Michael Culshaw-Maurer

