Hey guys,

Just figured it out- I needed to transpose my data, and then tidyr::gather worked like a charm.

Here's the breakdown of what I did:

Enter code here...d <- as.data.frame(d)

dt <- t(d)

colnames(dt) <- dt[1,]
dt <- dt[-1,]

dt <- as.data.frame(dt)

setDT(dt, keep.rownames = T)[]

colnames(dt)[1] <- "Run"
colnames(dt)[4:53] <- c(seq(1,50,1))

dtg <- gather(dt, Time, Count, 4:53)

dtg$Run <- gsub("\\.[0-9]*$", "", dtg$Run)

dtg <- arrange(dtg, Run, InfectionStatus, Time)

dtg

I'm sure there's likely a more elegant way to go about doing this, but it seemed to work fine, and I've got the data organized just how it should be.

Cheers,

Michael

